# @repository    https://github.com/Novaking34/OmniCode_Framework
# @system        OmniCode Big House — Sovereign Multi-Machine Alignment Topology
# @role          Pins First-Party Sovereign Submodules at Root Without Melting History
# @maturity      Rev 5 Baseline | v0.1.3 Mass Alignment Wave
# @chassis       gitlink-registry | Sovereign standalone machines mounted as gears
# @scale         O(1) deterministic commit-pinned alignment across sibling repos
# @seams         in: FaithNet (Go FNP/1), Tenebris-and-Lux (C23/Rust/Python)
# @invariants    1. Universal 5-Block Lifecycle Protocol (Rev 5).
#                2. Every mounted submodule remains a standalone, independently
#                   runnable machine ("a machine becomes a big gear, yet every cog
#                   remains a cog").
#                3. Space-free root paths (`FaithNet`, `Tenebris-and-Lux`) keep
#                   Go, CMake, Cargo, and shell toolchains clean during alignment.
#                4. External-domain downstream consumers (e.g., `yugioh-server`)
#                   stay strictly OUTSIDE this manifest to preserve clean framework
#                   decoupling and IP boundaries.
#
# PURPOSE & ARCHITECTURAL ROLE:
#   Mounts CreativeWorkzStudio LLC's first-party sovereign sibling machines at
#   the OmniCode root so cross-track seams (DAR diagnostics, Tryte5/FNP/1 wire
#   parity, 5-Block validation, and the Rust AI chassis) are directly visible
#   and alignable while preserving each repo's independent git history and build.
#
#   ### For Everyday Builders & Contributors:
#   Clone the whole house in one command:
#     git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/Novaking34/OmniCode_Framework.git
#   Or initialize submodules after cloning:
#     git submodule update --init --recursive
#
#   ### For Systems Programmers & Engine Architects:
#   - `FaithNet/` supplies the zero-dep Go FNP/1 networking substrate & Tryte5 seam.
#   - `Tenebris-and-Lux/` supplies the zero-heap Cornerstone C23/C11 engine,
#     first-party RPG proving ground, Rust 5-Block validator lab, and Python AI
#     exoskeleton slated for gradual graduation into OmniCode core.
# ==============================================================================

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 2: OPENING BLOCK
# ( Submodule Alignment Conventions & Branch Tracking Policy )
# ==============================================================================
# Branch tracking rules:
#   - `FaithNet` tracks upstream `master` (Novaking34/FaithNet).
#   - `Tenebris-and-Lux` tracks upstream `main` (Novaking34/Tenebris-and-Lux).
# Recommended host Git settings (enabled globally on workstation):
#   submodule.recurse = true | status.submodulesummary = 1 | diff.submodule = log

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 3: BODY BLOCK
# ( Mounted Sovereign Submodule Declarations )
# ==============================================================================

[submodule "FaithNet"]
	path = FaithNet
	url = https://github.com/Novaking34/FaithNet.git
	branch = master

[submodule "Tenebris-and-Lux"]
	path = Tenebris-and-Lux
	url = https://github.com/Novaking34/Tenebris-and-Lux.git
	branch = main

# ==============================================================================
# BLOCK 4: AUDIT PROCEDURES BLOCK
# ( Submodule Integrity & Pointer Verification )
# ==============================================================================
# Pre-flight verification commands:
#   1. Inspect pinned commit hashes and clean checkout state:
#        git submodule status
#   2. Validate `.gitmodules` INI syntax via Git config parser:
#        git config --file .gitmodules --list
#   3. Confirm zero detached/dirty drift across all gears:
#        git submodule foreach 'git status -sb'

